---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro'
import { LINKS, SITE } from '../../consts'

/*
 * Obligations page.
 *
 * The FFmpeg and TMDB notices below are required, not decorative. FFmpeg's
 * compliance checklist names websites explicitly; TMDB's API terms specify the
 * notice wording verbatim. Do not paraphrase either.
 */
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Licences & attribution"
  description="Licensing for Playarr Server and Playarr, the FFmpeg and TMDB notices the project is required to display, and its trademark and patent position."
>
  <Section eyebrow="Legal" title="Licences and attribution">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="playarr">Playarr Server and Playarr</h2>
      <p>
        Playarr Server's and Playarr's own source code is released under the MIT licence.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>Copyright (c) 2026 Thomas McFarlane</p>
        <p>
          Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this
          software and associated documentation files (the “Software”), to deal in the Software
          without restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify, merge,
          publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit
          persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:
        </p>
        <p>
          The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all copies or
          substantial portions of the Software.
        </p>
        <p>
          THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED “AS IS”, WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
          INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
          PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE
          FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR
          OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER
          DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        The full text is in the <a href={LINKS.licence} rel="noopener">repository</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="ffmpeg">FFmpeg</h2>
      <p>
        This is an important distinction and worth stating plainly: <strong>{SITE.name}'s own
        source is MIT-licensed, but the published container images additionally bundle FFmpeg,
        which is licensed under the GNU General Public Licence version 2 or later.</strong> The
        image as a whole is therefore distributed subject to that licence.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>
          This software uses libraries from the FFmpeg project under the GNU General Public Licence
          version 2 or later. FFmpeg is a trademark of Fabrice Bellard, originator of the FFmpeg
          project. {SITE.name} is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or the owner of FFmpeg.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        FFmpeg runs on the server as a separate process. It is <strong>not</strong> embedded in any
        Playarr client application.
      </p>
      <p class="todo">
        <strong>Corresponding source.</strong> Anyone distributing a Playarr Server container image must
        make the exact corresponding FFmpeg source, and the build configuration used, available
        alongside the binaries. This page is where those links belong, per published image tag.
        They are not yet published here. If you need them before they are, please
        <a href={LINKS.issues} rel="noopener">open an issue</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="tmdb">TMDB</h2>
      <p>
        <img src="/_site/tmdb-logo.svg" alt="TMDB" width="212" height="18" loading="lazy" />
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>
          This website uses TMDB and the TMDB APIs but is not endorsed, certified, or otherwise
          approved by TMDB.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote>
        <p>This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        The first notice applies to this website. The second applies to Playarr Server and the
        Playarr apps. Metadata identifiers and artwork reaching a Playarr Server installation may
        originate with TMDB, by way of the library-management tools it reads from or the metadata
        sources the operator configures. TMDB is not a partner, sponsor or
        endorser of this project.
      </p>

      <h2 id="patents">Codecs and patents</h2>
      <p>
        Media codecs may be covered by patents in some jurisdictions. Nothing on this site, and no
        licence granted by this project, conveys any patent rights. Deploying this software
        commercially, or distributing builds of it, may require a separate patent licence depending
        on where you are and what you are doing. No claim is made that operating Playarr Server is
        royalty-free.
      </p>

      <h2 id="third-party">Other third-party software</h2>
      <p>
        Playarr Server and the Playarr apps include the open-source and vendor components below.
        Each remains under its own licence, and each project's own licence text applies. Exact
        versions are pinned in the dependency manifests and lock files in the
        <a href={LINKS.repo} rel="noopener">repository</a>, which are authoritative.
      </p>

      <h3>Playarr Server (Rust)</h3>
      <p>
        The server is built from Rust crates. The project's licence policy accepts only these
        licence families: MIT, Apache-2.0 (including with the LLVM exception), BSD-2-Clause,
        BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Unicode-3.0, Zlib, CC0-1.0, MPL-2.0, NCSA, CDLA-Permissive-2.0 and
        BSL-1.0. Most are permissive. MPL-2.0 (used by option-ext, for example) is file-level
        copyleft: changes to the MPL-licensed files themselves must be shared under the MPL.
        The direct dependencies include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Runtime and web: tokio, tokio-util, futures, async-trait, axum, axum-server, tower, tower-http, reqwest, rustls, rustls-acme, rustls-pki-types, instant-acme, x509-parser</li>
        <li>Data and API: sqlx, serde, serde_json, uuid, chrono, chrono-tz, toml, utoipa, utoipa-axum</li>
        <li>Authentication and cryptography: jsonwebtoken, argon2, ed25519-dalek, chacha20poly1305, sha2, hmac, hex, base64, rand_core, ipnet</li>
        <li>Backup and storage: age, tar, flate2, zip, fs4, tempfile</li>
        <li>Caching and search: moka, dashmap, strsim, unicode-normalization, fastembed (and the ONNX Runtime it uses)</li>
        <li>Images: image</li>
        <li>Command line, errors and telemetry: clap, anyhow, thiserror, tracing, tracing-subscriber, tracing-appender, tracing-opentelemetry, opentelemetry, opentelemetry_sdk, opentelemetry-otlp, libc</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Playarr for Android and Android TV</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>AndroidX (Core, Lifecycle, Activity, Navigation, DataStore, Room, WorkManager, Hilt integration, Core Splashscreen, TV Foundation and TV Material), Jetpack Compose and Material 3 (Apache-2.0)</li>
        <li>AndroidX Media3 / ExoPlayer (Apache-2.0)</li>
        <li>Dagger Hilt (Apache-2.0)</li>
        <li>Retrofit, the kotlinx.serialization converter for Retrofit, and OkHttp (Apache-2.0)</li>
        <li>kotlinx.serialization and kotlinx.coroutines (Apache-2.0)</li>
        <li>Coil (Apache-2.0)</li>
        <li>ZXing core (Apache-2.0)</li>
        <li>Firebase Cloud Messaging (Apache-2.0)</li>
        <li>The Google Cast framework and the Play In-App Updates library, supplied by Google under Google's own terms</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Playarr for iPhone and iPad</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Google Cast SDK for iOS, supplied by Google under Google's own terms</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Fonts (Android, iOS and web apps)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Nunito Sans and JetBrains Mono, under the SIL Open Font Licence 1.1. Copyright 2016 The Nunito Sans Project Authors (https://github.com/Fonthausen/NunitoSans); copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors (https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono). These notices apply to the Android, iOS and web apps.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Embedding model</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The server downloads the all-MiniLM-L6-v2 sentence-embedding model from Hugging Face on first use (<a href="https://huggingface.co/Qdrant/all-MiniLM-L6-v2-onnx" rel="noopener">model card</a>, ONNX port of <a href="https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2" rel="noopener">sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2</a>). Both model cards state the licence as Apache-2.0 (verified from the cards). The model is not bundled in the image.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Playarr web, admin and television web apps (TypeScript)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>React and React DOM (MIT)</li>
        <li>React Router (MIT)</li>
        <li>Shaka Player (Apache-2.0)</li>
        <li>openapi-fetch (MIT)</li>
        <li>qrcode (MIT)</li>
        <li>jpeg-js (BSD-3-Clause)</li>
        <li>Firebase JavaScript SDK, used for browser notifications (Apache-2.0)</li>
        <li>Google Cast sender SDK for the web, loaded from Google at run time under Google's own terms</li>
        <li>Scalar API Reference, used in the admin app (MIT)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>This website (Astro)</h3>
      <p>
        The direct production dependencies of this site. A CI check keeps this list in step with
        <code>package.json</code>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li data-pkg="astro">Astro (MIT)</li>
        <li data-pkg="@astrojs/mdx">@astrojs/mdx (MIT)</li>
        <li data-pkg="@astrojs/sitemap">@astrojs/sitemap (MIT)</li>
        <li data-pkg="sharp">sharp (Apache-2.0), used at build time for image processing; its prebuilt libvips binaries are LGPL-3.0-or-later</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Container images</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>FFmpeg, installed in the server image from the Debian distribution (GPL-2.0-or-later, see above)</li>
        <li>Debian base image packages, including ca-certificates, curl and tini, each under its own licence</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        The Xbox mark on the clients pages is the “xbox” brand icon from Font Awesome Free, used under
        CC BY 4.0. Other platform marks are from Simple Icons (CC0-1.0).
      </p>

      <h2 id="trademarks">Trademarks and affiliation</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
        sponsored by Sonarr, Radarr, Lidarr, Bazarr, Prowlarr, Readarr, Tdarr, Plex, Jellyfin,
        Emby, Apple, Google, Microsoft (Xbox), Amazon (Fire TV), Huawei (HarmonyOS), LG, Samsung,
        Hisense, Roku, or TMDB. All trademarks are the
        property of their respective owners, and are used here only to describe
        interoperability.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    scroll-margin-top: 90px;
  }

  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  blockquote p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .todo {
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
</style>
